        "statement": "Counterexamples exist for every $N\\ge3$. For the distributions in\nTheorem~\\ref{thm:main}, $S_\\alpha(q)>S_\\alpha(p)$ holds exactly for\n$0\\le\\alpha<\\alpha_*$, where $\\alpha_*>1$ is the unique root above one of\n\\begin{equation}\n (9/4)^{\\alpha_*}+7\\,4^{-\\alpha_*}=4.\n\\end{equation}\nHere $S_0$ is log support size and $S_1=\\HH$;\nnumerically $\\alpha_*\\simeq1.262623$.\nNo dimension-independent additive correction repairs the Shannon bound.",
